Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/lib/apps.c
Line: 3285
Function: corrupt_signature
Bug type: out-of-bounds-write
CWE: CWE-787
Explanation: Writes to s[signature->length - 1] without checking that signature->length > 0. If length is 0, this indexes -1 and writes before the buffer (and signature->data may be NULL when length is 0), causing a heap out-of-bounds write or NULL dereference.

